// Rule: [T1059.006][T1036.008] Starland RAT - Pythonw License Loader
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.006, T1036.008
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Hunting query - campaign-specific artifact
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR / Microsoft Sentinel with MDE tables
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: pythonw.exe executes a compiled loader disguised as LICENSE.txt.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for pythonw license loader using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A match indicates the exact runtime and masqueraded filename relationship described by the source.
// A match does not prove: Python bytecode content, decryption, Starland execution or ClickFix initial access.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Title: Starland RAT Python Loader Masquerading as LICENSE.txt
// Status: Hunting query - campaign-specific artifact
// Confidence: High
// Platform: Microsoft Defender XDR / Microsoft Sentinel with MDE tables
// Telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Hunt for pythonw.exe executing the source-observed compiled Python
// loader masquerading with a text-file name.
// ATT&CK: T1059.006, T1036.008
// Limitation: The filename is mutable and may be hidden by an execution wrapper.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName =~ "pythonw.exe"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "LICENSE.txt"
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName, AccountName,
          FolderPath, ProcessCommandLine,
          InitiatingProcessFileName,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
          SHA1, ReportId
